4768	REG-1741272815611	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972	Civil Rights	20 U.S.C. §§ 1681 - 1688		Title IX prohibits sex-based discrimination in any school or other education program that receives federal funding. This includes discrimination based on gender identity and sexual orientation. It covers a wide range of issues, including but not limited to admissions, recruitment, financial aid, academic programs, student treatment and services, counseling and guidance, discipline, classroom assignment, grading, vocational education, recreation, physical education, athletics, housing, and employment.	Educational institutions are required to comply with a wide range of requirements, such as adopting and publishing grievance procedures, designating one employee as a Title IX coordinator, not discriminating on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity, promptly responding to any complaints of sex discrimination, and ensuring that no person is retaliated against for opposing an unlawful educational practice or policy, or made the victim of a different form of discrimination.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:53:35.611	2025-03-06 14:53:35.611	2026-03-06 14:53:35.611	\N		https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights (OCR)					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4773	REG-1741273073877	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972	Civil Rights	20 U.S.C. §§ 1681–1688		Title IX is a federal law that prohibits discrimination based on sex in educational institutions that receive federal funding. This includes discrimination in all aspects of education such as admissions, athletics, and other school activities. It also addresses sexual harassment, sexual assault, and any gender-based discrimination that may deny a person access to educational benefits and opportunities.	Educational institutions are required to adopt and publish grievance procedures for students to file complaints of sex discrimination, to designate a Title IX coordinator to oversee the school's duties under Title IX, and to notify all students and employees of the name or title, office address, email address, and telephone number of its Title IX coordinator. Institutions are also required to respond promptly and effectively to sexual harassment and sexual assault complaints and to take steps to prevent recurrence and remedy its discriminatory effects on the complainant and others.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:57:53.877	2025-03-06 14:57:53.877	2026-03-06 14:57:53.877	\N		https://www.ed.gov	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights (OCR)					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4475	REG1796	Regulation E: Electronic Fund Transfers	Accounting	15 U.S.C. § 1693b	1583	Establishes the basic rights, liabilities and responsibilities of consumers who use electronic fund transfer services and of financial institutions that offer these services.\n\nAdditional Information:\nAn employer must pay social security taxes on employees but an exemption exists for most students also working for the University, for clergy whose services are performed in the exercise of their ministry, and for professional employees as defined in 26 CFR § 31.3121(b)(10)-2.\r\n\r\n \tTo avoid penalty for reporting incorrect SSN on W-2 forms, transmit data file electronically to the Social Security Administration (SSA). Report all employees hired in the specific quarter listing name (as it appears in HR System), SSN, sex, and date of birth. After information is queried against SSA's database, mismatches are sent back for resolution.	No specific requirements provided	Finance	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:29:50.616	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4476	REG1797	Sarbanes Oxley Act of 2002 (SOX)	Accounting	Public Law No. 107-204	1754	Designed to protect investors by improving the accuracy and reliability of corporate disclosures made pursuant to the securities laws.\r\n\r\n \tDoes not apply to public entities but may represent best practices.\r\n\r\n \t18 U.S. Code § 1519 makes destruction, alteration, or falsification of records in federal investigations, bankruptcy, or any matter within the jurisdiction of a federal department or agency a crime punishable by fines and up to 20 years imprisonment, and applies to all individuals, not just publicly traded corporations.\r\n\r\n \tBars independent auditors from providing certain non-audit services to the client institution.\n\nAdditional Information:\nImposes a 1.4 percent excise tax on the net investment income of private institutions that:\r\n\r\n \tHave at least 500 students\r\n\r\n \tHave more than 50% of students located in the U.S.\r\n\r\n \tHave assets valued at the close of the preceding tax year of at least $500,000 per full-time student.	No specific requirements provided	Finance	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:29:50.903	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
