4765	REG-1741272408230	Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act 2024 Update	Student Privacy	20 U.S.C. § 1232g; 34 CFR Part 99		This regulation protects the privacy of student education records and gives parents certain rights with respect to their children's education records. In 2024, changes were made to clarify the requirements for educational institutions and improve the protection of student's data.	Educational institutions must provide parents with access to their child's education records, allow parents to request the correction of records they believe are misleading or incorrect, and obtain written permission from parents before releasing any information from a student's education record.	Academic Programs	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:46:48.23	2025-03-06 14:46:48.23	2026-03-06 14:46:48.23	\N		https://www.ed.gov/	U.S. Department of Education		Office of the Chief Privacy Officer					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
