4535	REG1906	Lilly Ledbetter Fair Pay Act of 2009	Discrimination	Public Law No. 111-2	1771	An individual subjected to compensation discrimination under Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, or the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 may file a charge within 180 (or 300) days of any of the following: 1) when a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice affecting compensation is adopted; 2) when the individual becomes subject to a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice affecting compensation; or 3) when the individual's compensation is affected by the application of a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice, including each time the individual receives compensation that is based in whole or part on such compensation decision or other practice.\r\n\r\n \tThe Act has a retroactive effective date of May 28, 2007, and applies to all claims of discriminatory compensation pending on or after that date.\n\nAdditional Information:\nAn individual subjected to compensation discrimination under Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967, or the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 may file a charge within 180 (or 300) days of any of the following: 1) when a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice affecting compensation is adopted; 2) when the individual becomes subject to a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice affecting compensation; or 3) when the individual's compensation is affected by the application of a discriminatory compensation decision or other discriminatory practice, including each time the individual receives compensation that is based in whole or part on such compensation decision or other practice.\r\n\r\n \tThe Act has a retroactive effective date of May 28, 2007, and applies to all claims of discriminatory compensation pending on or after that date.	No specific requirements provided	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:04.686	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4493	REG1803	Title IX	Athletics	20 U.S.C. §§ 1681-1688	1633	Requires that no person shall on the basis of sex, be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, be treated differently from another person, or otherwise be discriminated against in any interscholastic, intercollegiate, club or intramural athletics offered by a recipient, and no recipient shall provide such athletics separately on such basis.\n\nAdditional Information:\nRequires that no person shall on the basis of sex, be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, be treated differently from another person, or otherwise be discriminated against in any interscholastic, intercollegiate, club or intramural athletics offered by a recipient, and no recipient shall provide such athletics separately on such basis.	No specific requirements provided	Academic Programs	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:29:54.35	\N	\N	\N		https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4769	REG-1741272828629	Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) Amendments Act of 2008	Civil Rights	42 U.S.C. § 12101 et seq.		The ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) is a wide-ranging civil rights law that prohibits, under certain circumstances, discrimination based on disability. The Act extends the mandate of the original Americans with Disabilities Act to include postsecondary institutions. It provides broader protections for disabled students and staff by extending the definition of 'disability', ensuring that a person is considered to be a person with a disability, and hence protected by the act, if they have a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits one or more major life activities.	Educational institutions must ensure accessible facilities and accommodation for students, staff and visitors with disabilities. This includes academic adjustments, auxiliary aids, services, or changes in policies or procedures that are necessary for disabled students to have an equal opportunity to participate in all academic and extracurricular activities. Institutions are also required to remove architectural, transportation, and communication barriers where such removal is readily achievable.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:53:48.629	2025-03-06 14:53:48.629	2026-03-06 14:53:48.629	\N		https://www.ed.gov	United States Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights (OCR)					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4770	REG-1741272841965	Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) 2024 Update	Education Rights	20 U.S.C. § 1232g		The 2024 Update to the Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) governs the access and privacy of student education records, further defining and protecting student rights. This update includes additional guidelines on digital and cloud storage data, as well as the sharing of data with third-party vendors in the context of online learning.	Educational institutions must ensure that education records are kept private and cannot be disclosed without student consent, except under specific circumstances outlined in the regulation. Institutions must adopt reasonable methods to verify the identity of parents, students, and school officials who request access to education records. They also need to provide annual notifications to students about their rights under FERPA. The 2024 update requires institutions to implement additional cyber security measures for digital and cloud-stored student records, as well as stricter data sharing agreements with third-party vendors.	Student Services	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:54:01.965	2025-03-06 14:54:01.965	2026-03-06 14:54:01.965	\N		https://www.ed.gov	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4774	REG-1741273084897	Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA)	Civil Rights	42 U.S.C. § 12101 et seq.		The ADAAA is a civil rights law that prohibits discrimination based on disability. It applies to public and private institutions that receive federal financial assistance and extends protections to students with disabilities to ensure equal access to education and services. It broadens the definition of 'disability' to cover more individuals.	Educational institutions must provide reasonable accommodations for students with disabilities, ensure that facilities are accessible, and cannot discriminate based on disability in any aspect of academic and extracurricular activities or services. They must also have a designated ADA compliance officer and a process for students to request accommodations and file complaints.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:58:04.897	2025-03-06 14:58:04.897	2026-03-06 14:58:04.897	\N		https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4821	REG-1741278267658	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; a Policy Interpretation; Title IX and Intercollegiate Athletics	Civil Rights	45 CFR Part 86		The regulation interprets Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, prohibiting sex discrimination in educational programs receiving federal assistance. It clarifies compliance requirements for intercollegiate athletics, including financial assistance, program areas, and meeting the interests and abilities of male and female students.	1. Compliance in Financial Assistance: Financial aid must be available on a substantially proportional basis to male and female participants. 2. Compliance in Other Program Areas: Male and female athletes should receive equivalent treatment, benefits, and opportunities in various program areas. 3. Compliance in Meeting the Interests and Abilities of Male and Female Students: Athletic interests and abilities of male and female students must be equally accommodated. Factors like coaching, facilities, and competitive opportunities should be equivalent.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 16:24:27.658	2025-03-06 16:24:27.658	2026-03-06 16:24:27.658	\N		https://www.ed.gov/about/offices/list/ocr/docs/t9interp.html#skipnav2	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
