4538	REG1908	Title IX of the Education Amendment of 1972	Discrimination	20 U.S.C. §§ 1681-1688	1633	Prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in education programs or activities receiving federal financial assistance, including employment.\r\n\r\n \tAny grievance records relating to a Title IX violation or complaint must be retained for the period of time cited in state law for personal injury actions.\n\nAdditional Information:\nProhibits discrimination on the basis of sex in education programs or activities receiving federal financial assistance, including employment.\r\n\r\n \tAny grievance records relating to a Title IX violation or complaint must be retained for the period of time cited in state law for personal injury actions.	No specific requirements provided	Academic Programs	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:05.311	\N	\N	\N		https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4540	REG1910	Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act (USERRA)	Discrimination	Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act (USERRA)	\N	Seeks to ensure that members of the uniformed services are entitled to return to their civilian employment upon completion of their service.\r\nQualified employees must be reinstated with the seniority, status, and rate of pay they would have obtained had they remained continuously employed by their civilian employer.\r\nThe law also protects individuals from discrimination in hiring, promotion, and retention on the basis of present and future membership in the armed services.\n\nAdditional Information:\nSeeks to ensure that members of the uniformed services are entitled to return to their civilian employment upon completion of their service.\r\nQualified employees must be reinstated with the seniority, status, and rate of pay they would have obtained had they remained continuously employed by their civilian employer.\r\nThe law also protects individuals from discrimination in hiring, promotion, and retention on the basis of present and future membership in the armed services.	No specific requirements provided	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:05.723	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4530	REG1901	Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967	Discrimination	29 U.S.C. §§ 621-634	1673	It is unlawful for the University to fail to hire, discharge, segregate, classify, or otherwise discriminate against any individual with respect to compensation, terms, conditions or privileges of employment because of age.\n\nAdditional Information:\nIt is unlawful for the University to fail to hire, discharge, segregate, classify, or otherwise discriminate against any individual with respect to compensation, terms, conditions or privileges of employment because of age.\n\nAdditional Information:\n<li style="list-style-type: none;">\r\n\r\n \tMakes it an unlawful employment practice for a covered entity to (1) deny reasonable accommodations to known limitations related to pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions, unless the entity can demonstrate an undue hardship; (2) require a qualified employee to accept an accommodation without engaging in an interactive process; (3) deny employment opportunities based on the need to make reasonable accommodations; (4) require a qualified employee to take leave if another reasonable accommodation can be provided; and (5) take an adverse action in the terms, conditions, or privileges of employment against a qualified employee because of a request for or use of an accommodation.	No specific requirements provided\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNot Applicable	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:05.93	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4778	REG-1741273213892	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972	Civil Rights	20 U.S.C. § 1681 & 34 C.F.R. Part 106		Title IX is a federal law that prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in any federally funded education program or activity. The law has been interpreted to include discrimination based on gender identity and sexual orientation. It also addresses sexual harassment, gender-based discrimination, and sexual violence in educational settings.	Educational institutions must establish and maintain policies against sex discrimination, sexual harassment, and sexual violence. They must also designate a Title IX coordinator to ensure compliance, promptly investigate any complaints of violation, provide equitable resolutions, and establish procedures for handling complaints. They must also provide educational materials and training for students and employees.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 15:00:13.892	2025-03-06 15:00:13.892	2026-03-06 15:00:13.892	\N		https://www.ed.gov	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights (OCR)					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
