4779	REG-1741273228277	Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) Amendments Act of 2008	Civil Rights	42 U.S.C. § 12101 et seq.		The ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) was enacted to reinforce protections for individuals with disabilities. The law expands the definition of 'disability,' thus increasing the number of people who are protected under the ADA. It applies to all aspects of higher education, including admissions, student services, and employment.	Educational institutions must ensure their facilities, programs, and services are accessible to individuals with disabilities. They must provide reasonable accommodations for students and employees with disabilities, unless doing so would fundamentally alter the nature of the service or program, or impose undue hardship. Additionally, institutions must not retaliate against individuals for asserting their rights under the ADA.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 15:00:28.277	2025-03-06 15:00:28.277	2026-03-06 15:00:28.277	\N		https://www.ed.gov	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights (OCR)					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
