4846	PA-paDep-1741804862430	Laws, Regulations, and Guidelines	Higher Education		\N	Department of Environmental Protection\nOur mission is to protect Pennsylvania’s air, land, and water resources while ensuring the health and safety of all residents and visitors to the commonwealth.\nStreamlining Permits for Economic Expansion and Development (SPEED)\nCreated to accelerate permit processing and keep Pennsylvania aligned with business demands, eligible permit applications will use DEP-approved contractors for expedited review.\nThe Invitation For Bids (IFB) is now open to find quali	Department of Environmental Protection\nOur mission is to protect Pennsylvania’s air, land, and water resources while ensuring the health and safety of all residents and visitors to the commonwealth.\nStreamlining Permits for Economic Expansion and Development (SPEED)\nCreated to accelerate permit processing and keep Pennsylvania aligned with business demands, eligible permit applications will use DEP-approved contractors for expedited review.\nThe Invitation For Bids (IFB) is now open to find qualified professionals to fill these roles.\nPopular\nLearn more about\n•\nClimate Change\n•\nPennsylvania Pipeline Portal\n•\nPFAS in Pennsylvania\n•\nDriving PA Forward\n•\nMethane Reduction Strategy\n•\nStormwater Management\n•\nBay Restoration\n•\nLead in Drinking Water\n•\nMine Subsidence Insurance\n•\nThe Environmental Regulatory Process in Pennsylvania\n•\nStream Maintenance\nNews releases\n•\nDEP to Host Public Hearing on North Centre Township HSCA Investigation in Columbia County\n•\nDEP Provides Update on Lancaster County Plane Crash Cleanup\n•\nShapiro Administration Holds Energy Transfer Accountable for Contaminating\n•\nShapiro Administration Launches RISE PA Initiative to Create Energy Jobs, Cut Costs, Grow Pennsylvania’s Energy & Manufacturing Industries, and Lower Toxic Air Pollution\nRISE PA will create thousands of good-paying jobs in construction and manufacturing – the $396 million program is for projects to reduce energy costs and air pollution from industrial facilities.\nUnion labor, environmental advocates, and leaders from across the energy industry have praised the Shapiro Administration’s commonsense efforts to create jobs and tackle industrial pollution while helping build healthier communities and a stronger economy in Pennsylvania.\n•\nAccessibility and discrimination\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Environmental Protection (DEP) works to make sure everyone can access its services. Learn more about how we do this by reading our policy.\nPAyback\nEligible for a refund of your permits, licenses, or certification application fees?​\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on Facebook\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on X\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on LinkedIn\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on Instagram\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on YouTube\n•\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Contact Us\n•\nMedia Inquiries\n•\nOpen Data Portal	Academic Programs	state	t	\N	\N	2025-03-12 18:41:05.182	2025-03-12 18:40:21.87	\N	\N	\N	https://www.dep.pa.gov	paDep	\N	paDep	https://www.dep.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	[{"url": "https://www.dep.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html", "type": "web-scrape", "lastChecked": "2025-03-12T18:40:21.870Z"}]	10	4846	2025-03-12 18:41:02.239691	\N	t	\N	PA	paDep	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4845	PA-paCHE-1741802622449	Certification Testing Requirements	Higher Education		\N	Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)\nOverview\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libra	Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)\nOverview\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libraries, and the State Library of Pennsylvania.\nCertification\nLogin to TIMS\n•\nClearances & Background Checks\n•\nContinuing Education and Professional Development\n•\nChild Labor Laws\n•\nSpecial Education\n•\nCertification Testing Requirements\n•\nAccessibility\n•\nTranscripts & Diplomas\n•\n2024-25 Education Budget\nTeach in PA\nEmpowerU\nFood & Nutrition\nCareer and Technical Education\nNew Releases\n•\nState Board of Higher Education to Embark on Statewide Stakeholder Engagement Tour to Help Develop Strategic Plan\n•\nShapiro Administration Highlights Commonsense Investments to Fight Food Insecurity at Millersville University\n•\nShapiro Administration Invites Nominations for National RISE Award to Honor Exceptional School Employees Across Pennsylvania\n•\nShapiro Administration Announces $300,000 to Educate Students Recovering at Home from Serious Medical Conditions\nContact Information & Affiliates\n•\nContact Us Form\n•\nContact by Phone\n•\nPDE Executive Staff\n•\nPDE Press Office\n•\nState Library of Pennsylvania\nCollecting, preserving, and providing access to materials for, by, and about Pennsylvania.\n•\nProfessional Standards and Practices Commission\nThe Professional Standards and Practices Commission sets preparation, certification, practice, and conduct standards for teachers.\n•\nState Board of Education\nThe State Board of Education reviews, develops, and adopts regulations that govern basic and higher education in the Commonwealth.\n•\nState Board of Higher Education\nProvide direction, coordination, and support to ensure that institutions of higher education fully meet the workforce and economic development needs of this Commonwealth.	Academic Programs	state	t	\N	\N	2025-03-12 18:41:23.67	2025-03-12 18:41:01.961	\N	\N	\N	https://www.education.pa.gov/Postsecondary-Adult/College%20and%20Career%20Education/Pages/default.aspx	paCHE	\N	paCHE	https://www.education.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	[{"url": "https://www.education.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html", "type": "web-scrape", "lastChecked": "2025-03-12T18:41:01.961Z"}]	26	4845	2025-03-12 18:03:42.482738	\N	t	\N	PA	paCHE	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4576	REG1847	Housing & Urban Development Lead Based Paint Poisoning in Certain Residential Structures	Environmental Health and Safety	42 U.S.C. § 4852d	1697	The University must provide lessees with a federally-approved pamphlet on lead poisoning prevention.\n\nAdditional Information:\nThe asbestos NESHAP regulations specify work practices for asbestos to be followed during demolitions and renovations of all structures, installations, and buildings (excluding residential buildings that have four or fewer dwelling units). The regulations require the owner of the building or the operator to notify the appropriate state agency before any demolition, or before any renovations of buildings that could contain a certain threshold amount of asbestos or asbestos-containing material. In addition, particular manufacturing and fabricating operations either cannot emit visible emissions into the outside air or must follow air-cleaning procedures, as well as follow certain requirements when removing asbestos-containing waste.	Annually, the University must provide a disclosure notice to lessees of property built prior to 1978 that such structures may contain lead based paint and/or lead based paint hazards, regarding the health risks of such hazard, and disclosing any known lead paint or hazard.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nThe University must comply regarding notices and permitting regarding the demolition of structures and waste removal.\nResources	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:14.149	\N	\N	\N	Annually, the University must provide a disclosure notice to lessees of property built prior to 1978 that such structures may contain lead based paint and/or lead based paint hazards, regarding the health risks of such hazard, and disclosing any known lead paint or hazard.	https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education							Annually, the University must provide a disclosure notice to lessees of property built prior to 1978 that such structures may contain lead based paint and/