4577	REG1848	Mandatory Reporting of Greenhouse Gases	Environmental Health and Safety	OSHA	1663	Implemented under the Environmental Protection Agency's (EPA) powers under the Clean Air Act, the rule requires that the university submit an annual report on the university's greenhouse gas emissions. Gases covered by the rule include carbon dioxide (CO2), methane (CH4), nitrous oxide (N2O), hydro fluorocarbons (HFC), per fluorocarbons (PFC), sulfur hexafluoride (SF6) and other fluorinated gases and hydro fluorinated ethers.\n\nAdditional Information:\nRequires employers to train employees on hazards in the workplace, to provide information to employees, to report occupational injuries and illnesses to the federal government, and to keep records of same, and to provide controls and protective equipment as well.	The University must submit an annual report on the University’s greenhouse gas emissions.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNo specific requirements provided	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:14.384	\N	\N	\N	The University must submit an annual report on the University’s greenhouse gas emissions.	https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education							The University must submit an annual report on the University’s greenhouse gas emissions.		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
