4590	REG3653	OSHA’s Occupational Exposure to Hazardous Chemicals in Laboratories Standard	Environmental Health and Safety			Provides strict guidelines for laboratory safety. Key components of the laboratory standard include having a chemical hygiene plan and providing employees with training and information. The laboratory standard applies to labs that:\r\n\r\n \tuse hazardous chemicals\r\n\r\n \tserve as workplaces where relatively small amounts of hazardous chemicals are used on a nonproduction basis\r\n\r\n \thazardous chemicals are manipulated on a laboratory scale\r\n\r\n \tuse multiple chemical procedures or chemicals\r\n\r\n \thave procedures not part of a production process\r\n\r\n \tuse protective practices and equipment to minimize the potential for employee exposure to hazardous chemicals\r\n\r\n\r\nThese hazardous chemicals include those regulated under 29 CFR 1910 subpart Z, and those defined under the Hazard Communication Standard, 29 CFR 1910.1200	Not Applicable	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2020-03-03 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N	Not Applicable	https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor							Not Applicable		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
