4596	REG1862	Toxic Substances Control Act	Environmental Health and Safety	15 U.S.C. § 2601-2629	1584	Regulates the use and disposal of certain chemicals, including PCBs used in electrical transformers. Must comply with regulations concerning use, service, storage, and disposal of transformers containing PCBs.\r\n\r\n \tThe Act requires the identification, inventory, marking and quarterly inspection of PCB transformers.	15 U.S.C. § 2607; 40 C.F.R. § 761.180: A written annual document log of the disposition of PCBs and PCB items must be prepared for each facility by July 1st, covering the previous calendar year (January through December). The written annual report, which summarizes the records and annual document log shall be submitted to the EPA Regional Administrator by July 15th of each year.	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2014-01-25 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N	15 U.S.C. § 2607; 40 C.F.R. § 761.180: A written annual document log of the disposition of PCBs and PCB items must be prepared for each facility by July 1st, covering the previous calendar year (January through December). The written annual report, which summarizes the records and annual document log shall be submitted to the EPA Regional Administrator by July 15th of each year.	https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education							15 U.S.C. § 2607; 40 C.F.R. § 761.180: A written annual document log of the disposition of PCBs and PCB items must be prepared for each facility by July 1st, covering the previous calendar year (January through December). The written annual report, which summarizes the records and annual document log shall be submitted to the EPA Regional Administrator by July 15th of each year.		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false},