4601	REG1864	House and Senate Gift Ban and Ethics Rules	Ethics	House and Senate Gift Ban and Ethics Rules	\N	Both the House and Senate have banned gifts from registered lobbyists or private entities that retain or employ them. Non-lobbyists can give gifts valued at less than $50, such as a meal at a briefing for a Member of Congress and their staff that is valued at less than $50 per person.\n\nAdditional Information:\nBoth the House and Senate have banned gifts from registered lobbyists or private entities that retain or employ them. Non-lobbyists can give gifts valued at less than $50, such as a meal at a briefing for a Member of Congress and their staff that is valued at less than $50 per person.	No specific requirements provided	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:18.686	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
