4605	REG1865	Arms Export Control Act of 1976	Export Controls	22 U.S.C. §§ 2751-2799aa-2	1640	Provides the authority to control the export of defense articles and services, and charges the President to exercise this authority. Executive Order 11958, as amended, delegated this statutory authority to the Secretary of State.\n\nAdditional Information:\nProvides the authority to control the export of defense articles and services, and charges the President to exercise this authority. Executive Order 11958, as amended, delegated this statutory authority to the Secretary of State.\n\nAdditional Information:\nPrimary statutory basis for the Export Administration Regulations, which regulate the export of certain § dual use § item, i.e. items that are capable of both civilian and military use.	No specific requirements provided\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNo specific requirements provided	Research	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:19.659	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
