4805	REG-1741277029018	Title IX and Intercollegiate Athletics Policy Interpretation 1979	Civil Rights	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; 45 CFR Part 86		Policy interpretation providing guidance on compliance with Title IX in intercollegiate athletics. Prohibits discrimination based on sex in educational programs receiving federal assistance. Includes factors for compliance in financial assistance, other program areas, and meeting interests and abilities of male and female students.	{"Compliance in Financial Assistance (Scholarships)":{"regulation":"45 CFR 86.37(c)","details":"Financial assistance should be available on a substantially proportional basis to male and female participants in the athletic program. Compliance measured by comparing aid available to male and female athletes."},"Compliance in Other Program Areas":{"regulation":"45 CFR 86.41(c)","details":"Male and female athletes should receive equivalent treatment, benefits, and opportunities in various program areas like equipment, coaching, facilities, and support services."},"Compliance in Meeting the Interests and Abilities of Male and Female Students":{"regulation":"45 CFR 86.41(c)(1)","details":"Athletic interests and abilities of male and female students must be equally accommodated. Selection of sports and levels of competition should effectively accommodate interests and abilities."}}	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 16:03:49.018	2025-03-06 16:03:49.018	2026-03-06 16:03:49.018	\N		https://www2.ed.gov/about/offices/list/ocr/index.html	Office for Civil Rights		Department of Health, Education, and Welfare					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "en