4556	REG1911	Cafeteria Plan Regulations	Employee Benefits	Cafeteria Plan Regulations	\N	A cafeteria plan is a written plan that allows employees to exclude from gross income certain types of employer provided benefits, such as accident and health insurance, group term and life insurance, and benefits under a dependent care assistance program.\r\nQualified scholarships or tuition reduction, educational assistance or deferred compensation may not be excluded from income.\r\nFor purposes of determining the taxable year of inclusion, any benefit described in paragraph (1) or (2) from the statute shall be treated as received or accrued in the taxable year of the participant or key employee in which the plan year ends.\n\nAdditional Information:\nA cafeteria plan is a written plan that allows employees to exclude from gross income certain types of employer provided benefits, such as accident and health insurance, group term and life insurance, and benefits under a dependent care assistance program.\r\nQualified scholarships or tuition reduction, educational assistance or deferred compensation may not be excluded from income.\r\nFor purposes of determining the taxable year of inclusion, any benefit described in paragraph (1) or (2) from the statute shall be treated as received or accrued in the taxable year of the participant or key employee in which the plan year ends.	No specific requirements provided	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:09.487	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
