4573	REG1844	Guarding and Use of Hand & Portable Powered Tools	Environmental Health and Safety	Housing & Urban Development Lead Based Paint Poisoning in Certain Residential Structures	1697	The University is responsible for the safe condition and guarding of portable powered tools/equipment (ex: saws/drills/drivers/sanders/grinders/ pneumatic tools/explosive fasteners, etc.) including tools furnished by employees.\n\nAdditional Information:\nThe University must provide lessees with a federally-approved pamphlet on lead poisoning prevention.	Annually, the University must provide a disclosure notice to lessees of property built prior to 1978 that such structures may contain lead based paint and/or lead based paint hazards, regarding the health risks of such hazard, and disclosing any known lead paint or hazard.	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:13.563	\N	\N	\N		https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4574	REG1846	Hazardous Materials Transportation Act	Environmental Health and Safety	49 U.S.C. §§ 5101-5128	1724	Primary objective is to provide adequate protection against the risks to life and property inherent in the transportation of hazardous material in commerce by improving the regulatory and enforcement authority of the Secretary of Transportation.\r\n\r\n \tTraining is required 90 days after employment or change in job function, followed by recurrent training once every three years.\n\nAdditional Information:\nImplemented under the Environmental Protection Agency's (EPA) powers under the Clean Air Act, the rule requires that the university submit an annual report on the university's greenhouse gas emissions. Gases covered by the rule include carbon dioxide (CO2), methane (CH4), nitrous oxide (N2O), hydro fluorocarbons (HFC), per fluorocarbons (PFC), sulfur hexafluoride (SF6) and other fluorinated gases and hydro fluorinated ethers.	University personnel who transport or cause to be transported hazardous materials must file annually a registration statement by June 30.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nThe University must submit an annual report on the University’s greenhouse gas emissions.	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:13.768	\N	\N	\N	University personnel who transport or cause to be transported hazardous materials must file annually a registration statement by June 30.	https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education							University personnel who transport or cause to be transported hazardous materials must file annually a registration statement by June 30.		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4570	REG1842	Energy Policy Act	Environmental Health and Safety	42 U.S.C. §§ 13201-13574	1702	Addresses energy production and contains Underground Storage Tank provisions.\r\n\r\n \tUnderground Storage Tank Training must be conducted every seven years.\n\nAdditional Information:\nThe University is responsible for the safe condition and guarding of portable powered tools/equipment (ex: saws/drills/drivers/sanders/grinders/ pneumatic tools/explosive fasteners, etc.) including tools furnished by employees.\n\nAdditional Information:\nThe University must ensure that no employee is exposed to an airborne concentration of asbestos in excess of 0.1 fiber per cubic centimeter of air as an eight hour time-weighted average. &nbsp;Applies to occupational exposure other than construction.\r\nThe University must perform initial monitoring where employees are or may reasonably be expected to be exposed at or above the exposure limit, and must promptly notify such employees of the results within 15 working days.\r\nRequired, repeated monitoring depends on the initial results. Additional safety and compliance procedures are required.	Underground Storage Tank annual registration and postings required September 1 of each year.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNo specific requirements provided\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNo specific requirements provided	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:14.818	\N	\N	\N	Underground Storage Tank annual registration and postings required September 1 of each year.	https://www.ed.gov	Department of Education							Underground Storage Tank annual registration and postings required September 1 of each year.		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submiss