4763	REG-1741272386164	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972	Prohibition of sex discrimination in educational programs	20 U.S.C. §§ 1681–1688	1701	Title IX is a federal law that protects people from discrimination based on sex in education programs or activities that receive Federal financial assistance. It states that no person in the United States shall, on the basis of sex, be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or be subjected to discrimination under any education program or activity receiving Federal financial assistance.\n\nAdditional Information:\nProhibits covered entities from discriminating on the basis of disability against a qualified individual in regard to recruitment, hiring, wages, promotion, and other employment-related matters.\r\n\r\n \tEnforced by multiple federal agencies, including the Department of Justice, Department of Labor, and the EEOC.\n\nAdditional Information:\nProhibits covered entities from discriminating on the basis of disability against a qualified individual in regard to recruitment, hiring, wages, promotion, and other employment-related matters.\r\n\r\n \tEnforced by multiple federal agencies, including the Department of Justice, Department of Labor, and the EEOC.	Educational institutions must ensure equal opportunities regardless of sex, must have established procedures for handling complaints of sex discrimination, and must have a Title IX coordinator to oversee compliance.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\nNo specific requirements provided	Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-07 15:52:14.873	2025-03-06 14:46:26.164	2026-03-06 14:46:26.164	[]		https://www.ed.gov	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pendi